---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Process from '../components/Process.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import Reviews from '../components/Reviews.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import ServicesGrid from '../components/ServicesGrid.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icons.astro';
import { SITE, CTA } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema, serviceSchema } from '../data/schema';

const path = '/ceramic-coating/';
const title = 'Ceramic Coating Oakland, CA | Applied at Your Home | J&W';
const description =
  'Professional ceramic coating in Oakland, applied at your home. Decontamination and paint correction included, then a coating bonded to the paint. Quoted per vehicle. 4.9★ Google.';

// The questions people actually ask before they buy a coating, answered
// straight. No lifespan promises: the expected life of the specific coating
// is part of the quote, because it depends on the product, the prep and how
// the car is washed.
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What does a ceramic coating actually do?', a: 'It bonds a hard, glass-like layer to your clear coat. Once cured, that layer takes the abuse the paint used to take: sun works on the coating instead of oxidizing the clear coat, bird droppings, tree sap and bug splatter sit on top instead of etching in, brake dust and road film cannot bond, and water beads and sheets off instead of drying into spots and grime. Because it goes on over freshly corrected paint, the finish also looks deeper and glossier, and the coating locks that clarity in. The everyday result is a car that stays cleaner longer, washes in half the time and keeps its colour.' },
  { q: 'Is a ceramic coating worth it?', a: 'For most people who keep a car more than a year and park it outside at least some of the time, yes. The value is not one big moment, it is hundreds of small ones: rinsing off a week of dust in five minutes, sap that wipes away instead of etching, paint that is still deep and unfaded when you sell or trade the car. It is worth the most on new or freshly corrected paint, dark colours, cars that live outdoors, and anyone who dislikes washing. It is worth the least on paint whose clear coat is already failing, which no coating can fix.' },
  { q: 'How long does a ceramic coating last?', a: 'A professional coating is measured in years, not months. How many depends on the grade of coating, how well the paint was prepared, whether the car is garaged, and above all how it is washed. Hand or touchless washing with a pH-neutral soap keeps it working; brush car washes, harsh chemicals and contamination left to bake all shorten it. When we quote your vehicle we tell you the expected life of the specific coating we will use, and exactly how to get all of it.' },
  { q: 'Does a ceramic coating stop scratches and rock chips?', a: 'No. A coating is a few microns thick. It resists the fine swirls that washing puts into paint and it shrugs off chemical damage, but it cannot absorb a rock at freeway speed, a key or a shopping cart. That is what paint protection film (PPF) is for: a thick, clear urethane film that takes the impact. Many owners do both, film on the hood, bumper and mirrors where chips happen, and a coating over the whole car for gloss, chemical resistance and easy cleaning. For a daily driver that is not always behind trucks on the freeway, a coating alone is usually the right call.' },
  { q: 'Do I need paint correction before a ceramic coating?', a: 'Yes. A coating locks in whatever is under it, so swirls, water spots and haze sealed beneath a coating stay there for its entire life. Correction removes them first, and a corrected, fully decontaminated surface is also what lets the coating bond properly to the clear coat. It is included in both of our packages: one-step polishing for newer or well-kept paint, two-step compounding and polishing for heavily swirled, oxidized or dark paint.' },
  { q: 'Can I coat a brand-new car?', a: 'It is the best time. New paint has the fewest defects to correct, and coating it before its first automatic wash means it never picks up the swirls most cars carry within a year. It still needs decontamination and a light polish, because transport, the dealer lot and the pre-delivery wash leave more behind than you would think. A professionally applied coating does not affect the manufacturer\'s paint warranty. If a dealership offers you a protection package, ask what product is applied and whether any correction is done before you pay for it. Teslas, Rivians and other cars with thin, soft paint benefit the most.' },
  { q: 'How do I wash a ceramic-coated car?', a: 'Gently and regularly. Two-bucket hand wash with a pH-neutral car shampoo and a clean microfiber mitt, every two to three weeks if the car lives outside, then dry it with plush microfiber towels or a blower rather than letting it air-dry. Touchless car washes are fine. Avoid brush and cloth tunnel washes, degreasers, and anything acidic or strongly alkaline on the paint. Do not put wax or a paint sealant over a coating; they cannot bond to it and only mask how it behaves. A maintenance detail once or twice a year keeps it performing.' },
  { q: 'Can I take a coated car through an automatic car wash?', a: 'Touchless, yes. Brush or cloth tunnels, no: the spinning brushes carry grit from every car before yours, and they are the fastest way to put swirls into a coating. If a touchless wash is your routine, dry the car afterwards, because the recycled water those systems use leaves mineral spots.' },
  { q: 'How long does the job take, and when can I drive and wash the car?', a: 'A complete coating with one-step correction is a full-day appointment. Two-step correction can run longer or split over two visits. You can drive the car the same evening. Keep it dry and out of direct rain, sprinklers and bird droppings for the first 24 hours while the coating hardens, and do not wash it at all for the first week; no soap, chemicals or waxes for two weeks. If it gets rained on early, dry it, do not scrub it. You get written cure and care instructions for the exact coating we used.' },
  { q: 'Will a ceramic coating stop water spots?', a: 'It makes them less likely and easier to remove, not impossible. Water spots are minerals left behind when tap or sprinkler water dries on the paint. A coating keeps them from bonding into the clear coat, but they can still etch the coating itself if left in the sun for weeks. Dry the car after washing, keep it away from lawn sprinklers, and wipe fresh spots with a quick detailer as soon as you see them. Caught early they come off; ignored, they need polishing.' },
  { q: 'What can damage a ceramic coating?', a: 'Abrasion and chemistry, in that order. Brush car washes, dirty wash mitts and dry wiping put fine scratches into it. Strong wheel cleaners, degreasers, tar removers and alkaline truck-wash soaps eat into it. Bird droppings, bug splatter and tree sap left to bake in the sun will etch through eventually. Neglect is the quiet one: a coating that is never washed gets buried in road film and stops beading, which people mistake for the coating failing. Regular gentle washing prevents all of it.' },
  { q: 'How do I know the coating is still working?', a: 'Water behaviour is the tell. A working coating beads tightly and sheets off when you rinse. When beading goes flat and the paint stays dusty after a wash, it is almost always road film sitting on top of the coating, not the coating wearing out, and a decontamination wash brings it back. When the paint stops beading even after a proper decontamination, the coating has reached the end of its life and it is time to correct and re-coat.' },
  { q: 'Can wheels, glass, trim, wraps or PPF be coated too?', a: 'Yes, with coatings made for each surface. Wheel coatings shrug off brake dust so wheels rinse clean instead of needing harsh cleaners. Glass coatings sheet rain off the windshield at speed and make bugs and ice easier to clear. Trim coatings keep black plastic dark. Wraps, paint protection film and matte paint can be coated with matte-safe products that protect without adding gloss. We quote these as add-ons to the paint.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between a spray-on ceramic and a professional coating?', a: 'Spray ceramics and ceramic-infused waxes are toppers: a thin layer applied in an afternoon that lasts a few months, with no prep. A professional coating is a far denser product applied panel by panel over corrected, decontaminated paint, then cured, and it protects for years. Sprays are a good way to maintain a professional coating between details. They are not a substitute for one.' },
  { q: 'What decides the price of a ceramic coating?', a: 'Three things: the size of the vehicle, because more panels mean more prep and more product; the condition of the paint, which sets whether one-step or two-step correction is needed; and how much you want coated beyond the paint, such as wheels, glass and trim. We quote every vehicle individually from its year, make, model and a photo of the paint in sunlight. A quote far below the going rate usually means the correction is being skipped, and correction is most of the work.' },
  { q: 'Do you come to me for ceramic coating? What do you need?', a: 'Yes. We apply coatings at your home or workplace across Oakland, Alameda, Berkeley, San Leandro, Piedmont, Emeryville, Orinda and Walnut Creek. We need a garage, carport or shaded driveway out of direct sun and rain, and about a day. We bring water, power and lighting.' },
];

const schema = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Ceramic Coating',
    description: 'Professional mobile ceramic coating in Oakland and the East Bay. Complete application includes decontamination, paint correction and a hydrophobic ceramic coating bonded to the paint, applied at your home or workplace.',
    path,
    image: '/images/ceramic-coating-oakland.jpg',
    offers: [
      { name: 'Silver Ceramic Package', description: 'Hand wash, clay & iron decontamination, one-step paint correction, professional ceramic coating, cure & inspection.' },
      { name: 'Gold Ceramic Package', description: 'Everything in Silver with two-step paint correction for heavily swirled or oxidized paint.' },
    ],
  }),
  faqSchema(faqs),
  breadcrumbSchema([{ label: 'Services', href: '/services/' }, { label: 'Ceramic Coating', href: path }]),
];

const steps = [
  { title: 'Deep clean & decontamination', text: 'Detailed hand wash, iron remover and clay bar across every exterior surface. Oakland cars collect brake dust from 880 traffic and fallout near the Port, all of it has to come off first.' },
  { title: 'Paint correction & surface prep', text: 'Machine polishing removes swirls and scratches so the coating locks in a flawless finish, not old defects. Then a panel-wipe removes every trace of oil so the coating can bond.' },
  { title: 'Ceramic coating application', text: 'The coating is applied panel by panel, leveled and checked under light. Paint, and optionally trim, wheels and glass.' },
  { title: 'Cure & final inspection', text: 'The coating flashes and bonds; we inspect every panel for high spots before handing the vehicle back with care instructions. Full cure over the next 24 hours; no washing for 7 days.' },
];
---

<Base {title} {description} canonical={path} {schema} ogImage="/images/ceramic-coating-oakland.jpg" preloadImage="/images/ceramic-coating-oakland.jpg">
  <PageHero
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Services', href: '/services/' }, { label: 'Ceramic Coating' }]}
    eyebrow="Professional ceramic coating · Oakland & East Bay"
    titleHtml="Ceramic Coating in Oakland, <em>a harder, glossier, easier-to-clean finish</em>. Applied in your driveway."
    text="A complete coating, not a spray-on: hand wash, clay & iron decontamination, paint correction, then a professional-grade ceramic coating bonded to the paint. By the owner, at your home or office, quoted per vehicle."
    note="Complete · incl. decontamination & paint correction · full-day appointment"
    image="/images/ceramic-coating-oakland.jpg"
    imageAlt="Ceramic coating being poured onto an applicator pad before a mobile application in Oakland, CA"
    bullets={['Resists UV, sap, bird droppings, brake dust and road film', 'Correction included: the coating seals a flawless finish, not old defects', 'Hydrophobic: water sheets off, dirt lets go, every wash is faster']}
  />

  <!-- Answer + pricing -->
  <section class="section" id="pricing">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Ceramic coating in Oakland</span>
        <h2 class="mt-0">What your coating quote depends on</h2>
        <p><strong>A complete ceramic coating from J&W is quoted per vehicle.</strong> The quote covers the entire job: deep hand wash, clay and iron decontamination, paint correction, and a professional-grade coating applied and cured at your home anywhere in Oakland and the East Bay. Vehicle size is the biggest factor: more surface area means more prep time and more product.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Vehicle type</th><th>What it means for the job</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><strong>Coupe / Sedan</strong></td><td>Least surface area, fastest prep</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Mid-size SUV / Crossover</strong></td><td>The most common booking</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Large SUV / Truck</strong></td><td>Up to 40% more product and labor</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Add: multi-step correction (Gold)</strong></td><td>Heavily swirled, oxidized or black paint</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Add: wheels, glass, trim</strong></td><td>Extend coverage for easier cleaning</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted)">A quote far below the going rate usually means the decontamination and correction are being skipped, and prep is the whole ballgame.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a href={CTA.href} class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" data-scroll-book><Icon name="calendar" /> {CTA.label}</a>
          <a href={`tel:${SITE.phoneE164}`} class="btn btn--ghost"><Icon name="phone" /> {SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <img src="/images/ceramic-coating-oakland.jpg" alt="Ceramic coating being applied to an applicator block before going onto the paint in Oakland" width="1080" height="1080" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Packages -->
  <section class="section section--dark" id="packages">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="center" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
        <span class="eyebrow">Packages</span>
        <h2>Silver or Gold, the difference is how much correction your paint needs</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2 pk" style="max-width:960px;margin-inline:auto">
        <div class="pk__card">
          <span class="pill">Silver</span>
          <h3>Complete Coating + One-Step Correction</h3>
          <p>For newer cars, well-kept daily drivers and lighter colors. Removes light swirls and restores most gloss before sealing it in.</p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Detailed hand wash & decon pre-soak</li>
            <li>Iron removal + full clay bar</li>
            <li>One-step machine paint correction</li>
            <li>Panel prep wipe</li>
            <li>Professional-grade ceramic coating on all paint</li>
            <li>Cure, inspection & care guide</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="pk__price">Quoted by vehicle size</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pk__card pk__card--gold">
          <span class="pill pill--gold">Gold</span>
          <h3>Complete Coating + Two-Step Correction</h3>
          <p>For heavily swirled, scratched or oxidized paint, black and dark colors, and anyone who wants show-level clarity locked in.</p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><strong>Everything in Silver, plus:</strong></li>
            <li>Two-step correction: compound + finishing polish</li>
            <li>Hologram & deeper scratch removal</li>
            <li>Extra inspection pass under LED light</li>
            <li>Optional: coated wheels, glass & trim</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="pk__price">Silver + two-step correction</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="center" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <a href={CTA.href} class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" data-scroll-book><Icon name="calendar" /> {CTA.label}</a>
        <p class="fud" style="justify-content:center"><Icon name="check" /> Quote by vehicle before booking · Applied at your home</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Process steps={steps} heading="Four stages, prep is where cheap coatings fail, so we don't skip it" eyebrow="Our process" />

  <!-- What a coating does -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">What a coating actually does</span>
        <h2 class="mt-0">Four things that change once your paint is coated</h2>
        <p><strong>It stops damage before it reaches the paint.</strong> A cured coating is a hard, chemically resistant layer on top of the clear coat. Bird droppings, tree sap, bug splatter, brake dust and industrial fallout sit on the coating instead of bonding to the paint and etching it, so they rinse or wipe off instead of leaving marks. UV works on the coating instead of oxidizing the clear coat, which is what keeps colour deep instead of chalky.</p>
        <p><strong>It makes the car dramatically easier to keep clean.</strong> The surface is hydrophobic: water beads, then sheets off, and takes loose dirt with it. Dust and road film have far less to grip. A maintenance wash takes half the time, needs less scrubbing, and puts fewer swirls into the paint, because you are barely touching it.</p>
        <p><strong>It locks in gloss.</strong> The coating is applied over paint that has just been corrected, so it seals a flawless, deep finish rather than old defects. Coated paint has a wet, reflective look that a topper cannot match, and it keeps it.</p>
        <p><strong>It protects the value of the car.</strong> Paint condition is one of the first things a buyer or a dealer looks at. A coated car that has been washed properly still presents like new years later, which shows at trade-in time.</p>
        <p>Oakland conditions make the case: salt air on anything parked near the water in Alameda or Jack London Square, sap in Rockridge and the hills, brake dust from 880, and strong sun most of the year. Two honest limits: a coating does not stop rock chips or deep scratches, that is paint protection film, and it is not maintenance-free, it just makes maintenance easy.</p>
        <h3>Who books a coating with us</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>New-car owners</strong>, coat it before the first swirl. Teslas, Rivians, Toyotas, BMWs.</li>
          <li><strong>Black & dark paint</strong>, Gold package, because dark paint shows everything.</li>
          <li><strong>Outdoor parkers</strong>, street-parked in Temescal, Berkeley or Emeryville, or a sunny driveway in Walnut Creek.</li>
          <li><strong>People who hate washing</strong>, coated cars rinse clean; a maintenance wash takes half the time.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="img-frame"><img src="/images/work-1.jpg" alt="Black sedan freshly ceramic coated by J&W Mobile Detailing in an Oakland driveway" width="1376" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Reviews limit={3} filterService="Ceramic" heading="What Oakland drivers say after their coating" />
  <Faq faqs={faqs} heading="Ceramic coating questions, answered straight" />

  <section class="section section--soft" id="quote">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Request a quote</span>
        <h2>Tell us year, make, model and color. We'll quote Silver vs. Gold.</h2>
        <p class="lead">If you can, add a photo of the paint in sunlight so we can see the swirl level. Quotes usually go out within the hour during business hours.</p>
        <p class="alt-book"><a href={SITE.booking} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{CTA.bookLabel} &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
      <QuoteForm heading="Ceramic coating quote" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServicesGrid exclude={path} heading="Other services we bring to your driveway" eyebrow="More from J&W" lead="" />
  <CtaBand title="Ready for years of gloss, without leaving home?" text="220+ five-star reviews · Owner-operated · Eco-friendly products · We come to you across Oakland & the East Bay." />
</Base>

<style>
  .pk__card { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .pk__card--gold { border-color: var(--gold); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(245,179,1,0.3), var(--shadow); }
  .pk__card h3 { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; font-size: 1.5rem; color: #fff; }
  .pk__card > p { color: #b9bec8; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .pk__card .checklist { color: #e7e9ee; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .pk__price { margin-top: auto; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.9rem; font-weight: 800; color: #fff; }
  .pk__price small { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 500; color: #b9bec8; }
</style>
